# Copy to `.env` and fill in any keys you have.
# All providers default to free/keyless sources. Keys below are OPTIONAL and
# unlock alternative providers that you can wire up later.

# --- Recommended: news / sentiment ---
# NEWSAPI_AI_KEY powers the `newsapi_ai` provider (NewsAPI.ai / Event Registry),
# first in the shipped news chain. Free plan: 2,000 tokens; one search for the
# last month's news costs one token, a full selection run makes about 150, and
# answers are cached for 24 hours. Key: newsapi.ai > Dashboard > "Your API key".
# NEWSAPI_AI_MAX_CALLS caps the searches per run (default 200).
NEWSAPI_AI_KEY=
# NEWSAPI_AI_MAX_CALLS=200

# FINNHUB_API_KEY powers the default `finnhub` news provider, which is the only
# news backend here whose terms permit automated access. Get a free key at
# https://finnhub.io/register and paste it below.
#
# Without it the pipeline still runs: `finnhub` fails fast (one warning, no
# network call) and the configured chain falls back to the keyless `yahoo_rss`
# feed. That feed is rate-limited hard from datacenter/VPN IPs, so if your
# sentiment columns come back empty, setting this key is the fix.
FINNHUB_API_KEY=

# --- Optional: broker option C (Interactive Brokers, read-only) ---
# trading-monitor --broker C reads your positions through IBKR's Flex Web
# Service. In IBKR Client Portal open Performance & Reports > Flex Queries:
# the gear next to "Flex Web Service Configuration" enables the service and
# generates the token; then create an Activity Flex Query with "Open Positions"
# at Lot level of detail (date format yyyyMMdd) and copy its query ID.
# The token can only READ reports; it cannot trade. Never commit .env.
IBKR_FLEX_TOKEN=
IBKR_FLEX_QUERY_ID=

# --- Optional: other financial data providers ---
# Free tier exists for each of these. None are required to run the default pipeline.
ALPHAVANTAGE_API_KEY=
FMP_API_KEY=

# --- Optional: additional news providers (not implemented yet) ---
NEWSAPI_API_KEY=
MARKETAUX_API_KEY=

# --- Runtime / logging ---
ASSET_SELECTION_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# Path to an alternative YAML config (overrides the default location).
# ASSET_SELECTION_CONFIG=configs/my_config.yaml

# --- Binary options module runtime ---
BINARY_OPTIONS_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# Path to an alternative YAML config (overrides configs/binary_options/default.yaml).
# BINARY_OPTIONS_CONFIG=configs/binary_options/my_config.yaml
